# Laam CRM — SaaS best practices

When building or changing features, prefer industry SaaS CRM norms. Do not invent parallel patterns.

## Multi-tenant & security
- Every business query is **org-scoped** (`organizationId`). Never leak cross-tenant data.
- Secrets (courier, SMS, payment keys) are **per-org**, encrypted at rest, **masked on GET**, never hardcoded or logged.
- Mutations require permissions; audit sensitive actions (status, courier book, SMS, payments).

## API ↔ UI honesty
- If the UI exposes a control, the API must honor it — or hide/disable the control.
- No fake success toasts for unimplemented endpoints.
- Mock/demo data only when `NEXT_PUBLIC_USE_API` is false; API mode must not show fabricated finance/P&L.

## Domain (order-centric ops)
- Status changes go through one service path (stock cut/restock, activity log, side effects).
- Courier: book/sync per provider; bulk actions call the same book path as single-order.
- Payments/COD: real ledger rows — never “mock paid” in live mode.
- Idempotent external calls where practical (courier book, SMS unique id).

## Data & errors
- Validate payloads (Zod / shared `@laam/types`).
- Return clear, actionable errors (whitelist, missing creds, invalid phone) — not bare `fetch failed`.
- Prefer soft-delete / recycle patterns already in the codebase over hard deletes.

## Product decisions (when owner is silent)
- Choose the safer, auditable option over convenience.
- Ship Pathao + Carrybee depth before adding more couriers.
- Prefer fixing misleading filters/stubs before new screens.
